detail.title:
Service Children are full time equivalent (FTE) number of pupils aged 4 and over as at 31 August @year0 in Reception to Year 11 (pupils aged 4 to 15 where National Curriculum year groups do not apply) as recorded on the October @year0 School Census who are either: 
 @bullet recorded as a Service Child at any point since January 2017 (known as Ever 6); or 
 @bullet in receipt of a War Pension Scheme (WPS) or Armed Forces and Reserve Forces Compensation Scheme (AFCS) pension from the Ministry of Defence (MoD) as a result of injury, illness or death caused by Service. FTEs are calculated on the same basis as the Dedicated Schools Grant.

Each Service Child will attract @britishCurrencySymbol335 through the Pupil Premium. For pupils in maintained primary schools, maintained secondary schools, maintained special schools and NMSS, funding will be passed on via the local authorities. For pupils in academies and special academies, the ESFA will pass funding directly to the setting. Service child pupil premium allocations will be based on pupils recorded on the October @year0 School Census who are either: 
 @bullet recorded as a Service Child eligible for the service child premium since the January 2017 Census; or 
 @bullet in receipt of a War Pension Scheme (WPS) or Armed Forces and Reserve Forces Compensation Scheme (AFCS) pension from the Ministry of Defence (MoD) as a result of injury, illness or death caused by Service.
